# School ERP — Security

## Layout

```
security/
├── jwt/
├── filter/
├── config/
└── service/
```

## Authentication

- Spring Security + JWT (access + refresh)
- Login identifiers: email, phone, username
- `BCryptPasswordEncoder`; never store plain passwords
- Role-based authorization; protect admin routes

## Redis

- Active JWT / refresh tokens, OTP, blacklist on logout
- OTP expiry: 5 minutes; rate-limit OTP requests
- Set TTL on refresh tokens and OTP; remove tokens on logout
- Keys via `RedisConstants` — no hardcoded key strings

## JWT

- No hardcoded secrets (use `application.properties` / env)
- Validate tokens against Redis; support invalidation on logout
- Do not log token values

## OTP

- Store in Redis only; do not log OTP values
- Use `OtpUtil` and shared validation patterns
